// a namespace-qualified call used as a whole statement, and a call whose result is discarded.
//
// the statement form was matched as `{identifier, open_paren}`, so `math::sqrt(9.0);` - which
// lexes as `identifier :: identifier (` - matched no branch and was reported as an unexpected
// token. the spec's own `mem::free($p);` could not be written.
//
// discarding the result was a separate stop: a statement had to leave the value stack untouched,
// but a call pushes its return value, so any non-void call statement tripped the assert
float64 $root = math::sqrt(16.0);
echo $root;

// as a bare statement, result discarded
math::sqrt(9.0);

// the same for a plain unqualified call
function twice(int32 $x) : int32
{
    return $x * 2;
}

twice(21);

echo 1;
